{"approved":false,"back_sample":null,"beam_size":2,"checks":{"no_residual_markers":true,"nonempty":true,"not_truncated":true,"protected_values":true,"translated":true},"context":"specific-heat-calculator UI copy.howAnswer","detected_language":"nb","format":"usefulverse-background-draft-v1","key":"specific-heat-calculator.copy.howAnswer","keys":["specific-heat-calculator.copy.howAnswer"],"locale":"nb-NO","model":"google/madlad400-3b-mt","raw_translation":"For en temperaturendring uten faseendring, bruk Q = m·c·ΔT, hvor Q er varmeenergi, m er masse, c er spesifikk varmekapasitet og ΔT er temperaturendringen.Blandingsmodusen antar konstante egenskaper og et ideelt isolert system med mindre du angir varmetap.","record_id":"aea3c0d5333e149f298afbda85148c0ebef118b5e8a9cc9873ec547768de9f44","revision":"fa184c675da0b5c9e1c8694fccd4e12e2d422094","run_id":"41185047487","seconds":0.8947371367499954,"source":"For a temperature change without a phase change, use Q = m·c·ΔT, where Q is heat energy, m is mass, c is specific heat capacity and ΔT is the temperature change. The mixing mode assumes constant properties and an ideal insulated system unless you enter heat loss.","source_commit":"0795f2ac94fd96942ab121fbeaaccf7766f584d4","source_hash":"58f5ef56917f18dfaeb1efbb580a92ee037185080b8182c3f9398f9cabbfb59f","status":"needs-review","translation":"For en temperaturendring uten faseendring, bruk Q = m·c·ΔT, hvor Q er varmeenergi, m er masse, c er spesifikk varmekapasitet og ΔT er temperaturendringen.Blandingsmodusen antar konstante egenskaper og et ideelt isolert system med mindre du angir varmetap.","truncated":false,"warnings":["language_detection"]}
